cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use these data, please cite them as below. Each database also has its
  own version number and citation on its page at theimr.org.
title: "Migration Jurisprudence from the South: databases of migration and labor law"
type: dataset
authors:
  - name: Institute for Migrant Rights
    website: "https://theimr.org/"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.24389324"
url: "https://theimr.org/databases/"
repository-code: "https://github.com/pranotoiskandar-collab/compmigrationlaw"
license: CC-BY-4.0
abstract: >-
  Open, coded data on migration and labor law from the perspective of the
  Global South: international, regional and national instruments (Migration
  Law Atlas, with a farmworker view), court decisions from Asia, Africa, the
  Middle East and Latin America, comparisons of destination states (Gulf
  States, East Asia, Southeast Asia) and countries of origin, migrant domestic
  workers, and government hate speech. Each row links to an official source
  where one is available. Published by the Institute for Migrant Rights.
keywords:
  - migration law
  - labor law
  - migrant workers
  - court decisions
  - comparative law
  - Global South
  - farmworkers
  - domestic workers
  - hate speech
